* Thu Aug 06 2026 Michael Stauber <mstauber@solarspeed.net> 5.2-35
- Modified ci4/app/Controllers/BaseController.php to add strict cache 
  validation for the System object. If the Redis cache entry is missing 
  any of the mandatory keys (OID, productName, productBuild, IPType, 
  gateway, gateway_IPv6), the cache is discarded and the object is 
  force-reloaded from CCE. This prevents sporadic 'Undefined array key 
  gateway' errors caused by incomplete stale cache entries.

* Mon Jul 13 2026 Michael Stauber <mstauber@solarspeed.net> 5.2-34
- Modified Libraries/CceClient.php to fix ActiveMonitor retrieval by using the API's
  direct GETOBJECT path in API mode instead of resolving through FIND first.
- Modified Libraries/BxPage.php to add null-safety so ActiveMonitor fallback logic
  no longer dereferences a missing object and crashes.
- Modified Libraries/BxPage.php to prevent 'Trying to access array offset on value
  of type null' errors when ActiveMonitor data is unavailable or incomplete.

* Mon Jun 22 2026 Michael Stauber <mstauber@solarspeed.net> 5.2-33
- Modified ci4/app/Controllers/BaseController.php to ignore CCEd-API restart.

* Mon Jun 22 2026 Michael Stauber <mstauber@solarspeed.net> 5.2-32
- Modified ci4/app/Controllers/BaseController.php to add extended liveness 
  check for cced-api. After the existing Unix socket liveness check, a new
  check tests whether cced-api is accepting TLS connections on its configured
  port. The check reads the listen address from /etc/cced-api/config/cced-api.conf
  (same as CceApiClient), cached in Redis for 2 seconds. If CCEd's socket is 
  alive but cced-api is dead, it runs systemctl restart cced-api.service in 
  the background. No need to unstuck the whole CCEd.
- Modified ci4/app/Libraries/CceApiClient.php to extend callApi() with retry 
  with backoff. If curl_exec() returns false (connection refused/timeout - 
  cced-api is down), the method now retries up to 3 times with a 1-second sleep 
  between attempts. On each retry, the stale curl handle is closed and re-
  initialized to get a fresh TCP connection. If all 3 attempts fail, it returns 
  null (instead of json_decode(false) which was null anyway, but now it's 
  explicit and logged).
- Modified ci4/app/Libraries/CceClient.php to extend getAll() with API 
  liveness check + socket fallback. Before routing through the API, getAll() 
  now calls isApiAvailable() (a quick ping). If the API is down, it falls through
  to the socket path (which uses find() + external_cce_get.pl). If the API is up 
  but returns null (all retries failed), it also falls through to the socket path. 
  Previously, getAll() would silently return an empty array when the API was down.

