* Fri Sep 10 2021 Michael Stauber <mstauber@solarspeed.net> 3.0-1BX44
- Modified ci/application/libraries/CCE.php as the function 'unescape'
  which parses data from CODB into a presentable format had issues
  with converting octals into UTF-8. The problem especially materialized
  if a sequence of octals had unexpected plain text numbers in them,
  which were then also made subject to conversion. As there usually 
  weren't enough numbers around to form a complete octal triplet, these
  errant numbers were then subsequently stripped out of the text that
  was supposed to be shown. As a solution the whole 'unescape' routine
  got overhauled to deal with this in a more adequate fashion. As an
  unexpected side effect this is also leaps and bounds faster, as we
  now directly return any text that doesn't have octals without further
  character-by-character processing.

