* Sun Nov 15 2020 Michael Stauber <mstauber@solarspeed.net> 3.0-1BX26
- Turns out the CodeIgniter CSRF protection is pretty garbage, as it
  doesn't take any difference between browser timezone and server
  timezone into account. When calculating short cookie expiry times
  this can be fatal, as the cookie set based on server timezone might
  already be expired according to the browsers timezone. To work around
  this issue a full heap of fixes had to be applied all over the place.
- Modified ci/application/modules/base/login/views/login_view_solo.php
  to have a new JavaScript calculate the difference between server and
  browser timezone and store that in a new cookie called 'tzoff'.
- Modified ci/application/modules/base/login/views/login_view.php
- Modified ci/application/modules/base/login/controllers/login.php to
  handle cookie 'tzoff' on successful login and to write a temporary
  file into Sausalito's capcache with the timezone offset. If that file
  cannot be written, we retain the cookie instead.
- Modified ci/system/core/Security.php to handle either the capcache
  tzoff file or in its absence the cookie to calculate a proper CSRF
  cookie expiry. With some exceptions and bells and whistles.
- Added etc/cron.hourly/bxalpine.cron to clean up capcache as needed.

